main=f'''<main><section class="book-detail"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/ebooks/">Digital books</a> / Garage conversion decisions</div><div class="book-detail-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Before committing to construction</span><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">{d['subtitle']}</p><p>26 pages · 4 hypothetical worked cases · 7 reusable worksheets · 35 fillable fields · 2 completed records</p><section id="buy-book" class="ebook-top-buy-panel"><p><strong>£{price} GBP</strong> · One-time purchase · English PDF.</p>{btn}<p><a href="#sample-pages">Preview 3 real pages before buying</a></p></section><section class="book-value"><h2>Prepare a decision you can explain</h2><p>{esc(d['outcome'])}</p><ul><li>Give the authority and designer a precise proposed-use question.</li><li>Record where displaced storage and parking functions go.</li><li>Distinguish garage footprint, retained zones and proposed room area.</li><li>Connect new findings to the funding gap and commitment gate.</li><li>Check parallel dependencies without treating a forecast as permission to occupy.</li></ul><h3>Who will find it useful?</h3><p>U.S. homeowners considering an existing garage conversion before committing to construction. Bring accessible property records and actual professional findings. If you need a permit decision, architectural plans, structural design, a rental-law determination or a current local cost estimate, obtain the appropriate qualified service.</p><h3>Start with the free article</h3><p><a href="/blog/{blog}">Questions to answer before budgeting a garage conversion</a> provides seven feasibility questions and a free area-denominator example. The book adds four complete worked cases, a staged decision packet, seven reusable sheets and two completed records.</p><h3>Related books and limitations</h3><p>{esc(d['overlap'])}</p><p>The <a href="/ebooks/home-addition-cost-planning-guide">addition guide</a> addresses broader ways to gain space. Buying both is optional. This book does not certify living area, approve occupancy, forecast rental income or recommend construction methods. Worksheet fields do not calculate. Usefulness and willingness to pay have not been tested with real readers.</p></section><h2>Actual PDF contents</h2><ol>'''+''.join('<li>'+esc(v['title'])+'</li>' for v in d['sections'])+'''</ol><h3>Seven reusable records</h3><ul>'''+''.join('<li>'+esc(w[0])+'</li>' for w in d['worksheets'])+f'''</ul><p>Two completed demonstrations show the same area and budget prompts filled with labeled invented data. The US Letter PDF has 35 interactive note fields, clickable references and outline navigation. Keep a blank master, save and reopen a completed copy in a compatible reader. Longer notes scroll; use attachments for detailed reports. Your PDF entries remain in your file.</p><p>The <a href="/calculators/contractor-quote-comparison">free contractor quote comparison tool</a> supports general scope checks after the feasibility questions are addressed.</p></div><aside class="book-detail-card"><img src="/assets/books/{slug}/cover.webp" alt="{title} actual PDF cover" style="width:100%;height:auto"><p class="book-price">£{price} GBP</p>{btn}<p>After paid checkout, use your private order page to download this book. Its matching thank-you email links to that order page. No account or subscription required.</p><p>Original edition · October 30, 2026. Project examples use invented USD. Personal use includes sharing completed records with your own providers; do not redistribute or resell the blank book.</p></aside></div><section id="sample-pages" data-real-pdf-preview="true"><h2>Real pages from this edition</h2><div class="ebook-sample-grid">'''+''.join(f'<figure class="ebook-sample-page"><a href="/assets/books/{slug}/page-{i}.webp"><img src="/assets/books/{slug}/page-{i}.webp" alt="Actual PDF page: {label}" style="width:100%;height:auto" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>{label}</figcaption></figure>' for i,label in [(1,'Gross area versus proposed room case'),(2,'Completed budget pause record'),(3,'Reusable budget and commitment gate')])+'''</div></section><h2>Source context</h2><p>Primary links checked October 30, 2026. Sources do not endorse this book.</p><ul>'''+''.join(f'<li><a href="{u}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{esc(n)}</a>: {esc(note)}</li>' for n,u,note in d['sources'])+f'''</ul><p>Proposed and implemented test price: £{price} GBP, below the initial £12.99 queue hypothesis. The focused decision workflow, checked cases and reusable records support a conservative trial price; page count and free sources alone do not justify the charge. Existing prices remain unchanged.</p></div></section></main>'''

schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Book','name':title,'description':desc,'numberOfPages':26,'inLanguage':'en-US','bookFormat':'https://schema.org/EBook','datePublished':d['date'],'dateModified':d['date'],'author':{'@type':'Organization','name':'HomeCostEngine Editorial Team'},'url':'https://homecostengine.com/ebooks/'+slug,'image':'https://homecostengine.com/assets/books/'+slug+'/cover.webp','offers':{'@type':'Offer','price':price,'priceCurrency':'GBP','availability':'https://schema.org/InStock','url':'https://homecostengine.com/ebooks/'+slug}}
